.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PLATD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm platd
.Nd RavenBSD Raspberry Pi 4 platform server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar fake
.Op Ar mailbox=handle:length gpio=handle:length rng=handle:length dma=handle:length
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
owns the Raspberry Pi 4 VideoCore mailbox, the GPIO/pinmux arbiter and the RNG200, and registers
the
.Dq plat:
scheme. It is the single owner of those platform resources so the EMMC2, GENET and audio
servers do not program the same registers.
.Pp
The mailbox property channel is bounded (16-byte aligned property buffers, tag and response-code
validation, and a finite full/empty poll). The tag set includes board model, revision, serial,
MAC, clock rate and power state.
.Pp
Opening
.Dq plat:gpio/<pin>
claims the pin with the open-file description as the lease. A second claim returns
.Dv EBUSY .
The descriptor is released by
.Xr close 2 ,
and the kernel delivers a CLOSE notification when the owning client dies, so the server reclaims
the pin. A CALL on the lease selects the pin function, pull and level.
.Pp
The
.Dq plat:rng
descriptor returns at most 256 bytes per read. The RNG200 status bits are checked before each
FIFO read; an empty FIFO returns
.Dv EAGAIN
instead of blocking the server loop.
.Pp
With the
.Ar fake
argument the deterministic fake backend is used; this is the QEMU test path. Otherwise the
supervisor must transfer the platform MMIO and DMA capabilities and pass their numeric handles.
.Nm
never maps a physical address itself and never requests
.Dv ADMIN .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/platd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/platd.toml
Service manifest.
.It Pa profiles/platd.toml
Build profile.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr randd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
